WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:03.480
- [Instructor] So which
of the following numbers

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:08.480
is greater, 1/3 or 1/5?

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.290
Pause this video and try to answer that.

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:16.470
All right, now let's
think about this together.

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:19.160
And the way that I can best think about it

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.070
is by visualizing them.

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:23.460
So let's imagine a whole.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:28.460
So this is a whole right over there.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.300
And then let's say that
this is another whole

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.720
right over there, I'm gonna
try to make these rectangles

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.770
about looking about the same.

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:38.380
And now, how would I represent 1/3?

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:41.310
Well, I would divide this whole
into three equal sections.

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:44.740
And so I'm gonna try to divide
it into three equal sections.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:47.180
So that's three equal
sections right over there.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.340
Now they're supposed to
be three equal sections,

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:52.300
these are hand-drawn so
give me a little slack.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:56.090
But one of these three equal
sections, well that's 1/3.

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:59.780
So that is 1/3 right over there.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.690
Now what about 1/5?

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:06.160
Well then I would try to divide
this in five equal sections.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:09.091
So one,

00:01:09.091 --> 00:01:11.190
two,

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:12.630
three,

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:13.670
four,

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:15.530
and five equal sections.

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:19.320
And so 1/5 would be just
one of these fifths.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:22.930
So it would be that right over there.

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:27.180
So when you compare it like
this, what's larger 1/3 or 1/5?

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:29.310
And if it isn't obvious just yet,

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:32.440
I could drag this one over,

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:34.750
so that we can compare them,

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:37.230
so that we can compare them directly.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:40.560
And you can see very clearly that 1/3

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:43.210
covers more of the whole,
it's a larger fraction

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:45.660
of the whole than 1/5 is.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:49.050
So 1/3 is greater than 1/5.

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:51.550
And so you might have noticed
an interesting pattern

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:54.300
or might start thinking about a pattern.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.570
You might have been tempted
when you saw the five here,

00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:01.570
five is larger than three,
but 1/5 is less than 1/3

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:04.150
or 1/3 is greater than 1/5.

00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:06.900
And that is generally true,

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:08.940
that the larger the denominator,

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:11.560
the smaller the fraction is going to be.

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:12.590
Why is that?

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:16.490
Because you're dividing your
whole into more equal chunks.

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:18.360
So if you're only dividing into three,

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:21.760
if it's one of three of the
whole, 1/3 of the whole,

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:24.140
or if it's one of three
equal chunks of the whole,

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:26.150
it's gonna be bigger than one of five

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:27.910
equal chunks of the whole.

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:29.718
And so based on this,

00:02:29.718 --> 00:02:33.220
how would you compare these two numbers?

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:38.220
How would you compare 2/3 to 2/5?

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:42.975
Well, same idea here.

00:02:42.975 --> 00:02:45.370
1/3 is bigger than 1/5,

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:48.980
so 2/3 is definitely going
to be bigger than 2/5,

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:49.813
and you can see it here.

00:02:49.813 --> 00:02:52.433
2/3 is that,

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:58.380
while 2/5 is that right over there.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:00.000
And I can do another example

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.320
where I haven't even drawn it out.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:06.400
How would you compare four over six

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:09.970
to four over eight?

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:12.403
So 4/6 versus 4/8?

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:15.550
Well, same idea.

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:18.330
1/6 is larger than 1/8.

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:21.970
1/6 is greater than 1/8,

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:24.570
because the denominator here is smaller.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:27.420
We have the same numerator,
but the denominator is smaller.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:30.070
So four of the bigger
things is going to be larger

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:31.630
than four of the smaller things.

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:35.093
So 4/6 is greater than 4/8.

